    "created_at": "2024-08-12T17:10:39Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-08-12T17:10:39Z",
    "body": "Why not instead have the spec instead require caching of the result of the HTTP-redirect fetch?\r\n\r\nIt’s not clear at all to me what value there would be for a UA to cache the 30x redirect responses themselves, if the UA is every time just going to load the 30x and then right away make a new request for the resource/response it redirects to?\r\n\r\nI mean, I realize the UA will (should) likely also have a cached response for the resource the 30x redirects to. But the required spec behavior still results in an additional request being made, for every 30x redirect, every time.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
