    "created_at": "2024-08-13T08:02:15Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-08-13T08:02:15Z",
    "body": "If I'm understanding correctly what you're suggesting then the request URL would not be updated and a bunch of security checks would not end up happening?\r\n\r\nFurthermore, a temporary redirect in particular might also change what it redirects to pretty frequently, more frequently than any final response might change.\r\n\r\nThere is probably some further short-circuiting possible for permanent redirects, but it would have to be build on top of what we have today I think as we would still have to update the request URL and things like that. And it's not entirely clear what the pay-off for the specification would be to describe such a mechanism.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
